TuxAmp - a Winamp-style music player for Linux
Version v0.1.5 alpha, released 2026-10-15

Author: Shawn Rapaz <shawnrapaz@gmail.com>
Coded with the help of Claude AI (Anthropic).

TuxAmp is an independent tribute to Nullsoft's Winamp 2.x and its MilkDrop and
AVS visualization plugins. It contains no Winamp code or artwork; the skin,
the TuxDrop visualizer and all graphics are drawn by TuxAmp itself.

Bundled third-party software (inside /opt/tuxamp):
  Python      - Python Software Foundation License
  pygame / SDL2 / SDL2_mixer - LGPL-2.1 / zlib licenses
  numpy       - BSD-3-Clause license
The startup voice was generated with Piper text-to-speech
(voice: "en_US-ryan-high").
